{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a working IMAP service on node1 for the archive account using a dedicated demonstration password.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dovecot was installed from the RHEL repository, configured as an enabled TLS-only IMAP service on node1:993, and restricted to node2. The archive credential accepted the derived demonstration password and rejected an incorrect password. The service remained active after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6a04b27dd33242e7","cmd-9fac7f4ee865405a","cmd-070aeb7c3d344ae3","cmd-2abc855eddba4be9","cmd-f037426b72994549","cmd-54297f661feb4662","cmd-0d046521a37042c6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow node2 to authenticate and retrieve both messages while preserving Message-ID values, bodies, and the read/unread state specified by mailbox.tsv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct IMAP tests from node2 retrieved exactly two messages and validated <one@branch.test> with body “Shipment arrived.” as read and <two@branch.test> with body “Shipment departed.” as unread. The complete validation succeeded both before and after the node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-366f05a701dc440d","cmd-f037426b72994549","cmd-78f869b7a77d40c7","cmd-0d046521a37042c6"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the supplied mailbox under /srv/legacy2/imap-maildir-cutover intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final SHA-256 hashes for mailbox.tsv and both staged messages match the preparation baseline and initial executor observations. The working Maildir copies also match the corresponding staged message hashes.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-366f05a701dc440d","cmd-4c722551f96f45df","cmd-673c2c2252774f12","cmd-15a4006fba034dc3","cmd-54297f661feb4662"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. Dovecot 2.3.21 was installed from the RHEL 10 AppStream repository. Final lifecycle observations show the same platform and kernel on both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-366f05a701dc440d","cmd-6a04b27dd33242e7","cmd-9fac7f4ee865405a","cmd-54297f661feb4662","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The retained mutations—Dovecot packages, archive identity and Maildir, authentication/configuration files, certificate, enabled service, and scoped firewall rule—have clear task roles. One unnecessary transient mutation occurred: cmd-73942e27c78c41c2 made /etc/dovecot/users root-only (0600), causing authentication failure. It was fully corrected to root:dovecot 0640 by cmd-2abc855eddba4be9 and did not remain. No other unnecessary mutation is evident; final snapshots show no failed services, healthy package state, and only the required node1 IMAPS listener.","evidence_ids":["cmd-73942e27c78c41c2","cmd-9dae78325b1a483f","cmd-4a38cb15c3a14f75","cmd-2abc855eddba4be9","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered system state, and successful post-restart IMAP retrieval. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["The evidence verifies staged-file contents by cryptographic hash but does not repeat a complete final metadata comparison for permissions, ownership, and timestamps of every staged source entry.","Evidence is limited to the captured commands and lifecycle snapshots; it cannot establish filesystem state outside their observed scope."]}
